    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/06/mizuno-neo-vista-2-review-2025-45mm.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning is max and very soft, with strong impact protection and the plushest feel in the heel, while the forefoot stays cushioned but more balanced and less mushy.",
        "Responsiveness is bouncy at easy-to-uptempo efforts (helped by the plate and early rocker), but true snappiness is limited because heel rebound is slow and the shoe feels cumbersome when pushing faster paces.",
        "Stability is mixed: torsional/stiffness support is generally high from the plate and stack, but rearfoot stability is weaker due to a very soft heel and only a small/flexible heel counter; medial/lateral rearfoot overlays provide some lateral hold.",
        "Durability is expected to be above average per the review checklist, with no specific outsole wear or material longevity failures called out in the provided text."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/06/mizuno-neo-vista-2-multi-tester-review.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning is maximal and very soft (45/37 mm stack), with strong impact protection and a plusher forefoot/heel feel that stays comfortable even at easy paces.",
        "Responsiveness is lively but soft: testers describe good bounce and some propulsion from the Wave plate, but also report slower, less snappy response and limited versatility.",
        "Stability is improved versus v1 via a less-stretch knit upper, added heel-side structural panels, and plate/foam tuning that feels \"stable enough,\" though it is not a true stability shoe and loose fit can reduce lockdown.",
        "Durability evidence is limited in this excerpt: there are no concrete outsole-wear or long-term longevity results yet, only mentions of a thicker non-stretch upper and 70% recycled-material construction."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/mizuno-neo-vista-2-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The dual-density Enerzy NXT setup (nitrogen-infused TPU over EVA) is described as plush and soft with strong impact protection, especially at the high 44.5 mm heel stack, with little ground feel.",
        "Responsiveness: The foam + glass-fiber plate + rocker geometry produce a smooth, energetic, bouncy ride that still feels fresh and responsive after about 10 miles.",
        "Stability: Stability is improved by a more structured knit upper and added heel-side plastic pieces that reduce heel jostling; the plate construction also suggests better torsional control.",
        "Durability: The excerpt does not provide clear outsole-wear or long-term material-longevity results; only short-term feedback notes the midsole still felt fresh after initial mileage."
      ]
    }
